  "title": "The Missing Circle Is a Hole",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "perception and hidden objects",
  "premise": "A museum guard must find the circle stolen from a three-shape display, but every search focuses on loose objects. Turning on a lamp reveals that the circle is the empty hole between two curved display pieces; the guard hangs the FOUND label around the gap.",
  "hook": "We found every object. Where is the circle?",
  "visible_action": "Guard lifts a square and triangle, searches behind plinths, shifts a lamp, and frames the circular negative space with a label.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Look at the spaces between objects as well as the objects.",
  "gate": "Verify that the final silhouette is genuinely circular in the rendered view; no general claim about visual perception performance.",
